Title: Christmas at Vance Hall
Order: 6
Production Code: 1x06

INT. VANCE ESTATE - DRAWING ROOM - NIGHT

AMB: a costume party in full swing, distant laughter

[[Molly Vance]] presides over Christmas preparations; [[Charlie Vance]] lounges through all of it. Talk turns, as it always does around [[Reuel Briggs]], to his gift for mesmerism.

CHARLIE VANCE
Give the company a specimen of your infernal art, Briggs. He can raise the dead, girls, I promise you.

AUBREY LIVINGSTON
(low)
Let up, Charlie. It's no joke.

To smooth it over, Aubrey offers a story of his own.

AUBREY LIVINGSTON (CONT'D)
My father was Dr. Aubrey Livingston too — owned a plantation, and a slave girl among the house servants named Mira, who he'd throw into a trance for the amusement of guests. One dinner, two years before the war, he called her out to perform. Instead of tricks, she prophesied — every man at that table dead or imprisoned, every woman a widow, "a down-trodden race" to rule the land. Word for word, it came true. My own father died a prisoner of war in Boston Harbor. He sold her within the year. Never heard of her again.

MR. VANCE
Wonderful, and terrible. The world is a strange place.

AUBREY LIVINGSTON
There's more truth in mesmeric phenomena than science likes to admit.

Molly, moved by the thought of the friendless patient in Reuel's care, makes a sudden decision.

MOLLY VANCE
Tomorrow we bring her here, Dr. Briggs. There's room enough in this house, and she shan't be friendless a day longer.

She will not be argued out of it. [[Dianthe Lusk]], still unaware of her own name's weight, is coming to live under the Vance roof.
